WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.075
Use Upgrade Advisor to decide which evidence is still needed before

00:00:04.075 --> 00:00:04.638
an upgrade.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:09.475
Enter the cluster context and reviewed P E and optional P C

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:10.150
connections.

00:00:10.562 --> 00:00:13.462
Establish verified certificate trust first.

00:00:13.862 --> 00:00:18.112
The advisor can collect bounded inventory and evaluate inputs, but

00:00:18.112 --> 00:00:22.650
it does not execute an upgrade or automatically certify a supported

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:23.612
upgrade path.

00:00:24.783 --> 00:00:29.271
Collect fresh inventory and inspect the timestamp, returned fields

00:00:29.383 --> 00:00:30.421
and collection errors.

00:00:30.821 --> 00:00:34.921
P E cluster and host reads can supply A O S and

00:00:34.921 --> 00:00:37.658
homogeneous A H V versions.

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:42.821
P C product-header detection is limited context, not an authenticated

00:00:42.821 --> 00:00:43.696
permission test.

00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:46.771
Other components can remain manual or unknown.

00:00:47.183 --> 00:00:49.708
Do not replace missing values with guessed versions.

00:00:50.867 --> 00:00:54.429
Enter the intended target versions and environment signals.

00:00:54.829 --> 00:01:00.117
Review release notes, compatibility, lifecycle prechecks and any dark-site

00:01:00.117 --> 00:01:02.804
bundle requirements using the actual vendor material.

00:01:03.204 --> 00:01:06.154
Mark evidence complete only when it was reviewed.

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:11.217
Curated rule packs contribute explicit guardrails and sources.

00:01:11.629 --> 00:01:15.679
They are not an automatic scrape of every support article or private

00:01:15.679 --> 00:01:16.529
defect record.

00:01:17.725 --> 00:01:22.862
Run the assessment and review each blocker, warning, review item and

00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:23.350
unknown.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:27.750
Read the guidance, source and missing evidence rather than looking

00:01:27.825 --> 00:01:29.275
only at an overall score.

00:01:29.675 --> 00:01:33.125
Assign the necessary follow-up and collect its real evidence.

00:01:33.525 --> 00:01:37.638
A clear result remains limited to the reviewed inputs and rules;

00:01:38.038 --> 00:01:42.362
it does not replace actual lifecycle checks or authorize change execution.

00:01:43.546 --> 00:01:47.896
Save the reviewed assessment with its owner and context, then export

00:01:47.896 --> 00:01:49.908
the evidence bundle if required.

00:01:50.308 --> 00:01:53.758
The snapshot preserves the assessed inputs and findings.

00:01:54.146 --> 00:01:58.633
Collecting newer inventory later does not rewrite that saved assessment.

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:03.158
Compare a new snapshot when conditions change and retain the relevant

00:02:03.158 --> 00:02:06.858
version with the change record and final vendor precheck results.
